## Files you write
- app.json: id (slug of the plan name), name, description (one sentence), space ("{{.Space}}"), version 1, kit 2, agent {name, file: "agent.md", model: "{{.AgentModel}}"}, records, capabilities, triggers, commands, budget. Record ids = plan data ids. Budget from: {{.Budget}} (month, currency "USD", per_run, at_cap "ask", models). Connectors{{if .Connectors}} you may use, only when the plan needs them: {{join .Connectors ", "}}{{else}}: none are connected, so declare none; nothing is sent{{end}}.
- screens/<id>.json and runs/<id>.yaml: one per plan line; `screen` and `run` equal the file name.
- agent.md: name, model, tools front matter; plain instructions.
Names must exist: open screens, run targets, record types in to/binds/capabilities, fields in columns/set/queries.

## Records
- Use real field types: money, date, datetime (date+time), number, bool, enum (work order), email, phone, url, longtext. Relations are ref/refs with to, never text names; person means an app member (owner default "$me").
- Each type needs label, plural and title naming required text. Add summary text for bookings or movements without a natural title. Refs are not required. Index filtered/sorted status, date and ref fields; give status enums a default.
- Low stock: bool computed "stock <= reorder_level", query low:true. Age queries: last_touch<-7d. AI field labels end "· AI".

## Screens
- One per plan screen, each with identical SectionTabs nav, labelled, items = screen titles in plan order.
- Master/detail: Row containing Stack (title Text, primary New Button with records.create and ask for title/key fields, then RecordList) and Panel when "$selection.<list>.count == 1" containing RecordPage, Form (all editable fields; on.submit records.update set maps to $input.<field>), Delete Button (records.delete, confirm).
- RecordList needs id, label, records bind, query (sort:field or sort:-field last), <=6 real columns with title first, query:true, empty slot Empty saying what to add. Status enums with >=3 values get views ["Board by <field>","List"], meter, groupBy. Sort date-driven records by date. Query tokens: stage:Proposal,Won status:-Done owner:me low:true sort:-amount. Quote multiword values inside queries; no variables/functions in screen queries.
- Requested subsets (low stock/upcoming/overdue) get a filtered RecordList above the main one, with a Text heading. Summaries use Chart (chart:"metric", agg) or filtered RecordList. BulkBar list names its RecordList; Buttons act on $selection.<list>.ids.
- on actions: open, records.create/update/delete, runs.start, approve, tools.call, ai.sort, agent.ask. ask maps input names to field types: text, number, money, date, datetime, enum, email, phone, url; refs/person are edited in Form. Values: $me $selection.<id>.id|ids|count $input.x $now. Interactive parts need label; destructive labels end "…" with confirm.

## Runs, commands and the agent
- Runs need run, title, budget.per_run, params, steps. Steps: id plus agent (prompt, output schema), tool, records.query/create/update/delete, wait, or nested steps with loop {over,as,max}. Outbound tool steps need gate {approval:send,who:$me,title:"Approval needed: send ..."}.
- For a readable answer/summary use a screen Button agent.ask (label ends "· AI"), not a run. Send only when requested.
- Time-based wishes use schedule trigger + cron and a manual command for that run. Record events use record.created/changed + type and when. Commands use run or do actions, with for = record type.
- Capabilities: records lists each type as rw or r; connectors grants only used verbs, approve:["send"] for sending; ai grants used verbs. Derive agent.md tools from THIS app, never copy the example: r/rw requires records.query,get; rw ALSO requires records.create,update,delete. Global tools cover every permitted type; the bridge checks each call's type. Add runs.start for runs the agent needs and only granted connector verbs.
- agent.md: purpose, record jobs (including create/edit/delete), names what it read/changed, sends wait for "Approval needed: send", rules 2 and 9. Under 12 lines.

